<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    The engine sidecar is a PyInstaller onefile binary: at launch its bootloader
    unpacks an embedded libpython3.13.dylib into a temp dir and dlopen()s it.
    That dylib comes from uv's CPython distribution and is adhoc/linker-signed,
    so under the hardened runtime (which both PyInstaller and Tauri enable when
    a signing identity is set) library validation rejects it:

      Failed to load Python shared library '.../_MEIxxxxxx/libpython3.13.dylib'
      ... (non-platform) have different Team IDs

    The sidecar then dies before writing a byte of JSON-RPC, and the app can
    only report it as "sidecar closed stdout". Re-signing the extracted dylib
    is not possible for onefile, so the process must opt out of library
    validation. This entitlement is permitted under notarization.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
